{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1481787-fomori-and-banes-question","id":1481787,"title":"Fomori and banes question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-23T15:06:15-07:00","id":1481787,"title":"Fomori and banes question","content":"Hi guys,<br /> <br /> So, question for you all. When you kill a fomori, what happens to the bane that possessed the human? Does the bane materialize back into the Umbra? So for example if you kill a Fomori on Earth and you have some Garou on the other side, does the bane that was attached to the fomori materialize on the other side to do combat with the Garou? <br /> <br /> This is probably a dumb question with an easy answer that I should know, but for some reason I am at a100% brainfart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23998-dynamiterave","name":"DynamiteRave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T15:49:27-07:00","id":1481791,"title":"","content":"I don't think there is a clear canonical answer. I've had this question too, and I can't remember getting a clear answer on this forum.<br /> <br /> What I use is that if the fomori is slain before the Bane leaves the body, the Bane discorporates and goes into slumber and will eventually reform somewhere in the very deep umbra that originally spawned it. So there is nothing for the Garou to do.<br /> <br /> However, the Bane could decide to leave the fomori's body before it is destroyed. If that happens, the person stops being a fomori and just becomes an extremely sick - and likely dying person - from the accumulated Wyrm taint and poisons or tumors the bane has been preventing from killing the body while it's been a fomori. The Bane &quot;pops&quot; into the local Penumbra and can then attempt to flee.<br /> <br /> That last option is something players find very annoying. They feel it robs them of a victory and the scene is prolonged as they attempt to chase down the Bane and slay it. So it is not something I do very often. <br /> <br /> I only do it if I have a story in mind. I say that Gafflings never do that. They always go down with the ship as it is part of their &quot;programming&quot; to do so. However, Jagglings are more intelligent and have more free will. They often have plans that don't involve slumbering for some unspecified amount of time. So I would only have the Bane attempt to flee if 1) this is not a normal fomori, but a more powerful or intelligent one that was running some kind of real plan, 2) I have a good scene in mind in the Umbra that would be worth the initial frustration of the players, and 3) it will change things one way or the other whether the Bane escapes or the PCs destroy the Bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T23:41:23-07:00","id":1481828,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if &quot;Possessed&quot; (the book) elaborated on this, but using &quot;Possession&quot; (the Charm) is only the beginning of becoming a fomori, iirc. Ultimately the bane and the human merge into a new being and there is no going back for the bane. One might ask &quot;Why would a bane limit itself like this&quot; and the answer would be &quot;Banes are alien beings and their outlook an preserving their existence might be different from a humans&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, I'd rule the bane is gone as an individual being already when the fomori dies. If the merger is incomplete and it is &quot;just&quot; a Possession (as per the Charm), then the bane reappears in the Penumbra.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> To elaborate, my take on this comes from page 14 of Freak Legion.<br /> There is, among other information, this:<br /> <i>A fomor (plural fomori) is a person (or sometimes an animal) which has been possessed by a Bane (a Wyrm spirit). Once the transformation into a fomor is complete, that person is no longer human. He is something else entirely. The Bane is permanently wedded to his body and soul - two beings become one symbiotic whole.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 05-24-2022, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T05:50:03-07:00","id":1481841,"title":"","content":"Here is what <u>Possessed</u> has to say about curing fomori and what happens to the Bane, &quot;To date, the only proven method of separating the Bane from its host is to kill the host. The Bane is<br /> then set free (and usually tries to flee the area).&quot; (p.20)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T05:15:32-07:00","id":1481912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grimjaws</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1481787-fomori-and-banes-question?p=1481841#post1481841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is what <u>Possessed</u> has to say about curing fomori and what happens to the Bane, &quot;To date, the only proven method of separating the Bane from its host is to kill the host. The Bane is<br /> then set free (and usually tries to flee the area).&quot; (p.20)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bSo does that conflict with what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a> shows in Freak Legion page 14? Is the bane perma welded to the human, or does it get a chance to escape through the Umbra? <br /> <br /> I guess my bigger question is: Is there a major difference between 'possession' and 'creating a fomori' in this regard? I thought that if a bane possesses a human long enough to make the transfer to becoming a Fomori, that bane is now attached to the human, like a symbiotic bond. But another ST told me that what you cited instead. <br /> <br /> Has this been addressed in any of the W20 books yet? I have the new BoTW but I didn't see anything in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23998-dynamiterave","name":"DynamiteRave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T06:22:16-07:00","id":1481914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DynamiteRave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1481787-fomori-and-banes-question?p=1481912#post1481912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bSo does that conflict with what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a> shows in Freak Legion page 14? Is the bane perma welded to the human, or does it get a chance to escape through the Umbra?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the context it does pose a conflict.<br /> Freak Legion is older than &quot;Possessed&quot; - doesn't make it automatically superseed the other, although most people assume the newer material is canon.<br /> <br /> I don't like the approach in Possessed. It basically would mean that garou would have to go to the penumbra whenever other garou attack formoi, to kill banes so they can't get away (with spirit combat and Re-Form charm being their own problem). It also means that an hostile entity is on the loose after the first fomori is killed that most garou can't perceive (for it would take Gifts or an action/Gnosis roll to peek) and that might be able to use Charms through the Gauntlet to affect the fight. Including possessing a garou.<br /> It makes fomori basically enemies you have to kill twice.<br /> If that was the case, for millenia, since the Defiler Wyrm's minions first found out that fomori can be a thing, the garou should have more readily available means to combat the banes.<br /> <br /> By the logic of &quot;Possessed&quot; a Fomori is akin to a living wyrm fetish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DynamiteRave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1481787-fomori-and-banes-question?p=1481912#post1481912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI guess my bigger question is: Is there a major difference between 'possession' and 'creating a fomori' in this regard? I thought that if a bane possesses a human long enough to make the transfer to becoming a Fomori, that bane is now attached to the human, like a symbiotic bond. But another ST told me that what you cited instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, any ST might have a different take, since obviously different authors had different ideas, and depending on what sourcebook the ST read or what one's take on this is, it can practically be different within the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T00:23:45-07:00","id":1482134,"title":"","content":"IMHO Freak Legion and Possessed can be treated as equal. The first one gives the definition of fomori, the second one tells what happens after its death. Plus there were a few fetishes which, used for attacking fomori, hurts the bane, not the host.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T13:46:51-07:00","id":1482194,"title":"","content":"Would you have an example for such a fetish?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T13:50:30-07:00","id":1482286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1481787-fomori-and-banes-question?p=1482194#post1482194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you have an example for such a fetish?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/78023-fetish-help?p=83362#post83362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is one Fetish spear in the Storyteller's Screen (2nd Edition): Spear of Aranakol, Level 5, Gnosis 8. Damage: +3, To hit: 6. If attack a Bane posessed person, the &quot;body&quot; remains unharmed, but the Bane gets the damage. A very handy stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's your example. It's from the short adventure called &quot;Treasures of the past&quot;, where characters are send to retrieve a few Croatan fetishes from the museum. I don't want to spoil the plot twist but I can tell you that it's an unique one. But if one could be created then a few more could be too. Also I vaguely remember Talen bullets (but can't remember where I saw that) that work the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 05-29-2022, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T22:31:09-07:00","id":1482348,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the fetish is referencing only to the Charm &quot;Possession&quot;, or if it is meant to actually harm the bane part of a fomori - since I believe in 2nd Edition they were supposed to be individeable after the possession turned into the merger...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T02:53:58-07:00","id":1482357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1481787-fomori-and-banes-question?p=1482348#post1482348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if the fetish is referencing only to the Charm &amp;quot;Possession&amp;quot;, or if it is meant to actually harm the bane part of a fomori - since I believe in 2nd Edition they were supposed to be individeable after the possession turned into the merger...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not specified. But, as it is Level 5 fetish so the same as p. ex. Grand Klaive, I always used it as a perfect weapon for fomori.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T03:11:58-07:00","id":1482358,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">There is a levle 3 gift that function the same way than the <i>Spear of Aranakol </i>exept its for ghost possession, not fomori. If it can be done for ghost I guess it can be done for fla\u00efels</span> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Ghost-Eating Technique (</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">W20 Changing Breeds, p.268)</span></span> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T03:23:58-07:00","id":1482361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1481787-fomori-and-banes-question?p=1482357#post1482357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not specified. But, as it is Level 5 fetish so the same as p. ex. Grand Klaive, I always used it as a perfect weapon for fomori.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the level, I'd assume it was meant for fomori. But unfortunately, we don't know what the authors head canon in regards to fomori was, when this was written. Would the host die, if the merger ends due tot the bane side being dead? Is he mentally broken, with or without the chance of healing? Is the host back to his self before he was a fomori?<br /> Are the physical changes that usually appear in fomori healed, remain or something else?<br /> <br /> This are answers the ST should have answers to before a player uses the fetish. For, I think, there isn't anything solid in the books...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T03:43:53-07:00","id":1482363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1481787-fomori-and-banes-question?p=1482361#post1482361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This are answers the ST should have answers to before a player uses the fetish. For, I think, there isn't anything solid in the books...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Theoretically the host should die if it's a fomori. On the other hand then this fetish would loose much of its power. So I say the host would live but mentally broken. And no, ST should not tell this to its players. Remember, this is an unique fetish which weren't used since Croatan tribe gone. Maybe specific ancestor spirits would know the answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T04:09:22-07:00","id":1482365,"title":"","content":"The spirit within the fetish might tell the character.<br /> <br /> But sure, if the fetish is found in-game, there is no obligation to tell. I was more thinking along the lines of character creation - if a player spends background points on it, the player should know, what is bought...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T13:25:08-07:00","id":1482400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1481787-fomori-and-banes-question?p=1482365#post1482365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if a player spends background points on it, the player should know, what is bought...</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case sure, the player should know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar